wolf3d-portable @PROJECT_VERSION@ - SDL3 GUI host
================================================

This folder is a minimal cross-platform GUI build. Keep the executable,
Wolf3D shared library, SDL3 shared library, and every other included shared
library together. WOLF3D-LIB.txt records the compiled audio drivers.

On Linux, the local shared libraries are discovered relative to this
executable, so SDL3 does not need to be installed separately. The package
still requires a compatible CPU architecture, ELF loader and libc baseline,
and the normal Linux desktop facilities used by SDL; it is not a universal
cross-distribution static binary. A build made against a distribution's SDL
package may additionally require the matching X11, Wayland, audio, or graphics
runtime libraries; the default pinned-SDL build minimizes those direct
dependencies and is recommended for redistribution.

Copy the files from one supported original game installation beside the
executable, then run wolf3d-sdl3. Alternatively, leave the data
elsewhere and pass --data PATH. Use --game WL1, WL6, SDM, SOD, SD1, SD2,
or SD3 when automatic selection is ambiguous.

Mouse hardware and SDL-compatible game controllers are detected automatically.
Use --mouse or --joy to force a device present, and --nomouse or --nojoy to
force it absent. An enabled mouse uses captured relative input and is released
when the game loses focus.

The host displays the original 320x200 framebuffer at the intended 4:3
display aspect ratio with nearest-neighbor scaling. SDL3 provides the
window, keyboard, optional mouse/gamepad input, and audio device access;
game behavior remains in the separate Wolf3D library.

Press F11 or Alt+Enter to toggle borderless desktop fullscreen. F11 is handled
only by the host and will not dismiss an in-game "Press a key" prompt.

Run with --help for complete game and host options (--sdl3-help remains an
alias). Use --opl
nuked|dbopl|silent to select an included audio driver and --sample-rate HZ to
change the preferred PCM rate.

SDL3 is distributed under the zlib license. When included, Nuked-OPL3 is
independently replaceable and distributed under LGPL-2.1-or-later. See the included
LICENSE.txt, LICENSES directory, and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt. The LICENSES
directory also identifies wolf3d-lib's GPL-2.0 license explicitly.
